{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme","id":857268,"title":"Fast Track to Elder: Diablerie Scheme","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-01T13:48:24-07:00","id":857268,"title":"Fast Track to Elder: Diablerie Scheme","content":"So, I was coming up with nefarious plots for some vampire background characters and happened upon: seeks to acquire power through serial Diablerie. An old main-stay, right? The twist with this one was to keep things hidden and &quot;safe&quot;, they plan to only Diablerize newly made vampires that no one will miss. Preferably those they've made themselves.<br /> <br /> Problem:<br /> -Making a new vampire costs a Humanity dot/level (&lt;grumble&gt;, but there it is). Making many new vampires in short time is thus the fast track to Draugr-hood.<br /> Solution:<br /> +Embrace Vampire A (results in 1 Humanity loss). Make/Trick/Force <i>that</i> vampire into Embracing others. Kindred can do it right after waking up, it seems, so a bit of lies, threats, and Dominate should be enough for the new Neonate. Since vampires start with 7 Humanity, that's 7 more exsanguinated corpses they can raise before they turn feral.<br /> <br /> Problem:<br /> -Diablerie only give you 1 Exp per Blood Potency, and newly Embraced vampires only have 1.<br /> Solution:<br /> +Quantity over quality. Since it costs a flat 5 Exp to raise Blood Potency now, you only need to Diablerize 5 of the &quot;fresh&quot; vampires above to raise yours 1 dot/level.<br /> <br /> The Plan and The Math: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Perfect the vampire control method of your choice. Dominate, Majesty, Jack Bauer-technique, etc.</li> <li>Capture a nice round 45 people or so. Maybe extras, because you are going to be craving Vampire Vitae for your Requiem, and minions are nice.</li> <li>Embrace Patient/Vampire Zero. You lose 1 Humanity, they rise with 7 and 1 Blood Potency.</li> <li>Force Vamp 0 to Embrace 7 people. As they are now a Draugr, Diablerie them at leisure. [Netting 1 Blood-Potency-only EXP]</li> <li>Force each of their children to Embrace at least 37 other people. Now they are all Draugr and can be Diablerized. [Netting you 7 more BP EXP, bringing you to 8]</li> <li>Diablerize each of <i>their</i> children. [Netting you 37 BP EXP, bringing you to 45 EXP that can only be spent to raise Blood Potency. But that's enough to buy <i>9 dots</i>, enough to catapult you from BP 1 to BP 10]</li> <li>Enjoy nearly every Kindred you meet covering before you (Predator's Taint), and your immense powers (BP 10 to applicable dice pools). Mitigate the effects of Tainted with self-inflicted Aggravated damage as you desire. Since all victims were BP 1, it might be ruled that the penalty is only 1, and it fades after a month (or only requires 1 A damage to discard). Or the ST drops 45 on your cheating carcass. That might take longer to neutralize.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> So... thoughts? Am I missing something, or is BP 10 really that easy if the character is fine with mass murder/damnation/soul-eating?<br /> <hr /><br /> I can't help but note this is really only possible with the changes in 2E. 1E would prevent the serial Embrace through WP-cost, and eliminate the neonate Diablerie benefit entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":".  1st Edition note. 04-01-2016, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T13:57:11-07:00","id":857273,"title":"","content":"you lose humanity for committing diablrie, so you'd be humanity 0 after 7 vamps and unplayable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T13:58:18-07:00","id":857274,"title":"","content":"Nope, it's a Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> Still, 45 checks would bring you down fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T13:59:20-07:00","id":857275,"title":"","content":"&quot;Diablerie is always a breaking point, regardless of the vampire\u2019s Humanity score.&quot; VtR2E<br /> <br /> Even if your GM allows the bonus from multiple touchstones for the roll (I don't, it's auto-detachment in my game), rolling three dice 45 times is going to bring you down pretty quick as well.<br /> <br /> Also, I think facing a breaking point ends the some of the conditions gained through Dominate uses, so there's some question on whether you can Dominate someone to diablerize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T14:03:10-07:00","id":857276,"title":"","content":"Yeah i got my 1e mixed with my 2e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T14:06:44-07:00","id":857278,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/7c/e9/9a/7ce99a76b6cfb36ace8b26369b7ddafa.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> One does not simply capture 45 people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T14:22:16-07:00","id":857287,"title":"","content":"The answer is simple. Be a member of Ordo Dracul and get its Scale &quot;Mass Embrace&quot; from the Coil of the Voivode.<br /> Now you can embrace undetermined amount of vampires for the Cost of 1 Humanity. Just make sure their restraints are top notch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T14:24:55-07:00","id":857288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857275#post857275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Diablerie is always a breaking point, regardless of the vampire\u2019s Humanity score.&quot; VtR2E<br /> <br /> Even if your GM allows the bonus from multiple touchstones for the roll (I don't, it's auto-detachment in my game), rolling three dice 45 times is going to bring you down pretty quick as well.<br /> <br /> Also, I think facing a breaking point ends the some of the conditions gained through Dominate uses, so there's some question on whether you can Dominate someone to diablerize.</div> </div> </div> </div>With multiple Touchstones, you are rolling 3 dice each time. Might be other ways to raise it even more (Like if it is for your Requiem). If you start taking Humanity hits, take a breather and work on it. Then return to the feast you set up.<br /> <br /> As for Dominate, you would be using it to force them to Embrace, not Diablerize. And Embrace isn't on the chart. Yeah, it's auto Humanity loss, but it isn't technically a Breaking Point. And high level/exceptional success Dominate let's you even force breaking points, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857278#post857278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One does not simply capture 45 people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, non supernatural groups can do so in the real world. Might not be <i>easy</i>, depending on your location, but knock over a bus or 3 and you should be there. And 45 people was just to demonstrate the upper limit needed to go from BP 1 to 10. If you are starting from a higher level, or don't need to reach 10, then the number drops, obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T14:31:35-07:00","id":857290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857287#post857287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answer is simple. Be a member of Ordo Dracul and get its Scale &quot;Mass Embrace&quot; from the Coil of the Voivode.<br /> Now you can embrace undetermined amount of vampires for the Cost of 1 Humanity. Just make sure their restraints are top notch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, the humanity loss is the easiest part to negate out of this, provided you can force/trick others to Embrace, which doesn't seem to be that hard for confused neonates. The real issue is the Humanity checks for serial Diablerie. Unless you <i>can</i> take a Bane for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T14:38:22-07:00","id":857293,"title":"","content":"Keeping a bunch of people captive and forcing them to kill each other and turn their corpses into monsters is going to take Humanity breaking points from all but the most obliging of Storytellers.<br /> <br /> If you're going to point to the Humanity chart to declare what is and isn't a breaking point, first look at the top where it says Sample Breaking Points and a little further where it explains that other acts should count depending upon their nature. The list is not all-inclusive.<br /> <br /> A much faster way would be to commit diablerie on 4 Blood Potency 10 vampires and a Blood Potency 5 one. Even if you lose your Humanity, you're not potentially losing 45 Humanity.<br /> <br /> This brings you other obstacles. It takes Willpower to commit diablerie, Willpower you're not getting back by resting or 'taking a breath.' It's Willpower you're going to have to get back by doing something out in the world, the world that's missing 45 people and full of vampires who don't approve of diablerie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-01-2016, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T14:52:46-07:00","id":857299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857293#post857293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keeping a bunch of people captive and forcing them to kill each other and turn their corpses into monsters is going to take Humanity breaking points from all but the most obliging of Storytellers.<br /> <br /> If you're going to point to the Humanity chart to declare what is and isn't a breaking point, first look at the top where it says Sample Breaking Points and a little further where it explains that other acts should count depending upon their nature. The list is not all-inclusive.<br /> <br /> A much faster way would be to commit diablerie on 4 Blood Potency 10 vampires and a Blood Potency 5 one. Even if you lose your Humanity, you're not potentially losing 45 Humanity.<br /> <br /> This brings you other obstacles. It takes Willpower to commit diablerie, Willpower you're not getting back by resting or 'taking a breath.' It's Willpower you're going to have to get back by doing something out in the world, the world that's missing 45 people and full of vampires who don't approve of diablerie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgot about the Willpower point cost, thanks.<br /> <br /> As for the 4 10s and a 5, those are harder to find and prey upon than a bunch of 1s.<br /> <br /> And yes, the very premise already supposes that you've already cast aside most scrupples. Though, depending on how you are forcing them (such as via a threat), you might not be considered doing it each time. And such a blackguard might already have Banes covering the qualifying Breaking Points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T15:14:59-07:00","id":857309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857288#post857288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, non supernatural groups can do so in the real world. Might not be <i>easy</i>, depending on your location, but knock over a bus or 3 and you should be there. And 45 people was just to demonstrate the upper limit needed to go from BP 1 to 10. If you are starting from a higher level, or don't need to reach 10, then the number drops, obviously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah, and two hobbits did literally walk into mordor. The Boromir &quot;One Does Not Simply&quot; image macro isn't meant to suggest that a thing is impossible, just that a thing is easier said than done, and likely has serious consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T15:19:26-07:00","id":857312,"title":"","content":"This sounds like an amazing antagonist plan to be experienced and foiled by players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T15:27:41-07:00","id":857314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857312#post857312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like an amazing antagonist plan to be experienced and foiled by players.</div> </div> </div> </div>The other problem is the end result is a sort of top-heavy vampire. They have high Blood Potency but only the Disciplines and Attributes they started with. A neonate could grab them, pull them into the sun and get back inside without harm while the diablerist is soot. Entering any form of vampire society is going to be hard with their obvious signs of diablerism, but also necessary as they now need to feast on Vitae. If you decided to be a loner and just pick away at vampire society you risk Vinculum and exposure, as you don't have the decades and centuries of experience an elder has gained establishing a network of people, supplies and resources.<br /> <br /> At least if you commit diablerie on elder vampires you are likely to get some new Disciplines out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-01-2016, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T17:07:41-07:00","id":857351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857312#post857312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like an amazing antagonist plan to be experienced and foiled by players.</div> </div> </div> </div> Especially if a PC finds that one of their Touchstones is among the 45.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T17:21:30-07:00","id":857357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857351#post857351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Especially if a PC finds that one of their Touchstones is among the 45.</div> </div> </div> </div>God Machine needs specific 45* people dead, so it feeds a desperate vampire with occult ritual that shields the vampire from breaking points as long as he kills these specific people in specific way. Figure out what connects victims of the mysterious serial diablerist and stop the chain before he reaches your Touchstone who is on the list! Either find the killer, or disrupt the circumstances to the point where GM doesn't want these people dead anymore and stops sustaining &quot;humanity protection&quot; of it's designated killer.<br /> <br /> *Actually, it only needs 43,64 people, but it rounded up to leave a margin of error and because rounding up is proper thing to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-01-2016, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T19:05:11-07:00","id":857397,"title":"","content":"Are you using blood beats in your game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T19:32:49-07:00","id":857405,"title":"","content":"This scheme in itself is very interesting. But what kind of vampire would actually try this out in the first place? I mean, I met at least two serial diablerists in the times I've played Vampire. If you are making a character that has done it multiple times, would Torpor apply to them? If so how?<br /> <br /> A Nosferatu of the Noktuku bloodline is an obvious diablerist character but what about a power-hungry Daeva that tried to put their finger in all of the pies? There are a lot of possibilities with it and I am mainly curious with what character you decided on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11528-dangerus-muyoko-project","name":"Dangerus-Muyoko-Project","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T19:59:10-07:00","id":857415,"title":"","content":"The Daeva En Bloodline would without a doubt try this even if he might get caught. There from the Ancient Bloodline Book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:04:22-07:00","id":857420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857415#post857415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Daeva En Bloodline would without a doubt try this even if he might get caught. There from the Ancient Bloodline Book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incredible. I'll read that as well. Thank you for that information. Now that is interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11528-dangerus-muyoko-project","name":"Dangerus-Muyoko-Project","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:09:09-07:00","id":857422,"title":"","content":"Easy? Maybe. I am playing a serial diablerist in one of my games. The addiction part is the worst. It makes you sort of snap on the people you don't want to. Like if you're meeting with the prince and decide you need to eat him..<br /> <br /> I have BP 8 right now and it's taken 8 vampires and 5 actual Exp and there were a few failed attempts... <br /> <br /> Not diablerizing is hard once you start...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:15:54-07:00","id":857429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dangerus-Muyoko-Project</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857420#post857420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incredible. I'll read that as well. Thank you for that information. Now that is interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite litlerly En are all about being an Diablerist for POWERS sakes. They gain greater benefits form Diablerie as well as lessening the down sides.<br /> Their gain more bloodline power as they increase their Blood Potency. At Blood Potency 10 they can litlerly steel other bloodline disciplines.<br /> Check them out there one of my favorite Bloodlines.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.thesubnet.com/portal/cod/vtr/ClanLineageEn.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.thesubnet.com/portal/cod/vtr/ClanLineageEn.html\" target=\"_blank\"> 401 Unauthorized </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.thesubnet.com/portal/cod/vtr/ClanLineageEn.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.thesubnet.com/portal/cod/vtr/ClanLineageEn.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","user":"Blakemikizuki","date":". 04-01-2016, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:22:25-07:00","id":857432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857429#post857429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quite litlerly En are all about being an Diablerist for POWERS sakes. They gain greater benefits form Diablerie as well as lessening the down sides.<br /> Their gain more bloodline power as they increase their Blood Potency. At Blood Potency 10 they can litlerly steel other bloodline disciplines.<br /> Check them out there one of my favorite Bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>THAT SOUNDS HORRIFYING! Also, that's the best idea for a non-sexual Daeva villain. I am surprised nobody made more En vampires seeing how powerful this is. I hope Vent0 makes his serial diablerist that particular bloodline because I think they'll have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11528-dangerus-muyoko-project","name":"Dangerus-Muyoko-Project","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T23:01:04-07:00","id":857524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857312#post857312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like an amazing antagonist plan to be experienced and foiled by players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Foul amaranth, thy name is Rafael Pope. I don't think he's canonically of the En bloodline, but it would make sense given his obsession with power and knowledge through amaranth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11527-hakamichi-kurloz-sir","name":"Hakamichi Kurloz, Sir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T05:08:52-07:00","id":857631,"title":"","content":"Well, for reference, the character who started this line of thought was already an Elder who was cast out of their prior Domain for having (finally) been proven to have committed Diablerie. They entered the Focus Domain (where the PCs/action takes place) during a period of relative turmoil, and because it had a large contingent of Unaligned to hide amongst. Their previous Diablerie only whetted their taste, as it were, and they were eager to continue their efforts/experiments/addiction. He triggered a few riots, and instigated a few serial murderers to hide his initial abductions amongst. He was also planning on using this to jump-start empower a few thoroughly dominated enforcers.<br /> <br /> I made the thread because when I was doing the math involved, it seemed frightfully small and &quot;easy&quot;. People are free to take what they want from here for their own villains, though the Humanity checks for Diablerie and Willpower costs (as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> pointed out), will make sure your serial Diablerist will need to pace themselves. <hr /><br /> This was also somewhat instigated/inspired by that one thread that discussed forcing the Embrace. I'll try to link to it when I have more time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":".  Remembered inspiration. 04-02-2016, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T05:15:23-07:00","id":857632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dangerus-Muyoko-Project</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857432#post857432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THAT SOUNDS HORRIFYING! Also, that's the best idea for a non-sexual Daeva villain. I am surprised nobody made more En vampires seeing how powerful this is. I hope Vent0 makes his serial diablerist that particular bloodline because I think they'll have fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had them as Ventrue, actually. Not that important, since they are dead (Final Death, barring the need/desire for a curve-ball) by now anyways. They were a historical figure used to flesh out some backstory and explain why to Domain is in the state it is now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T07:31:22-07:00","id":857689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857314#post857314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The other problem is the end result is a sort of top-heavy vampire. They have high Blood Potency but only the Disciplines and Attributes they started with. A neonate could grab them, pull them into the sun and get back inside without harm while the diablerist is soot. Entering any form of vampire society is going to be hard with their obvious signs of diablerism, but also necessary as they now need to feast on Vitae. If you decided to be a loner and just pick away at vampire society you risk Vinculum and exposure, as you don't have the decades and centuries of experience an elder has gained establishing a network of people, supplies and resources.<br /> <br /> At least if you commit diablerie on elder vampires you are likely to get some new Disciplines out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting that the diablerist can pick up a whole load of skill dots. They might not pick up many new Disciplines (Do new vampires spontaneously manifest disciplines as part of the Embrace, or is it something that it's assumed a new character has trained in before play begins?) but those skill dots could be a big help. <br /> <br /> Careful selection of the victims would let you get to at least 4 dots in a few useful skills, like politics, which will seriously help you establish yourself. <br /> <br /> Definitely something I'd love to see an NPC do - It's a great antagonist for the PCs to disrupt, and an interesting start to a Chronicle could be the PCs escaping from someone trying to do this. And that drawback of being a &quot;top-heavy&quot; vampire as nofather said would make them a pretty good opponent to relatively young vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T14:00:43-07:00","id":857906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857689#post857689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Do new vampires spontaneously manifest disciplines as part of the Embrace, or is it something that it's assumed a new character has trained in before play begins?) but those skill dots could be a big help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disciplines are not trained. They do manifest spontaneously. They aren't taught, though I imagine practice helps. Indeed, the text seems to suggest that raising a Discipline is a meta decision that the <i>player</i> has a say in, but the <i>character</i> has no control over. At least in 2e, I can't speak for any other editions. How quickly they manifest is unclear, but given each Clan generally has at least one Discipline that allows them to feed much easier, I'd probably say they show up pretty darn quick as a survival mechanism from the Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T14:43:38-07:00","id":857934,"title":"","content":"Actually it says clan specific disciplines require a teacher. Dominate, majesty, Auspex, nightmare and ... Protean? <br /> <br /> Can't remember what page it says that on...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T14:50:14-07:00","id":857938,"title":"","content":"45 mortals are now missing and there's a fresh face on the scene whose aura absolutely reeks of diablerie.<br /> <br /> You're going to be up to your ass in hunters and taking you down is going to be priority number one for the local domain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T14:58:00-07:00","id":857946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857934#post857934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually it says clan specific disciplines require a teacher. Dominate, majesty, Auspex, nightmare and ... Protean?<br /> <br /> Can't remember what page it says that on...</div> </div> </div> </div>They require that you drink the blood of someone who knows them. They don't require a teacher. Here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire the Requiem 2e pg125</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Learning Disciplines<br /> Many Kindred spontaneously manifest new Disciplines, as<br /> the Beast asserts itself in new and strange ways. The Blood<br /> makes strong connections between vampires, so most Kindred<br /> only display the Disciplines of their Clan. To learn another<br /> clan\u2019s unique Discipline, the vampire must first track down<br /> another vampire who possesses the Discipline and drink at least<br /> one point of his Vitae \u2014 with all of the attendant consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T15:00:29-07:00","id":857948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857934#post857934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually it says clan specific disciplines require a teacher. Dominate, majesty, Auspex, nightmare and ... Protean?<br /> <br /> Can't remember what page it says that on...</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to taste blood of that Clan at least once and that's it. I think it's mentioned in description of starting Disciplines, something in vein of &quot;spend your 3 points here, and you may even buy a Clan Discipline of another Clan! But if you do, try to think how could i get your fangs on their blood!&quot;, my memory says.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T20:25:00-07:00","id":858106,"title":"","content":"Perfect! I was remembering wrong but this helps. I knew you had to drink the blood but for some reason it was stuck in my head that they needed to teach you too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T22:53:25-07:00","id":858171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857938#post857938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">45 mortals are now missing and there's a fresh face on the scene whose aura absolutely reeks of diablerie.<br /> <br /> You're going to be up to your ass in hunters and taking you down is going to be priority number one for the local domain.</div> </div> </div> </div>This plan would probably work best in some place that still has relatively isolated populations that might disappear without anybody really finding out or caring. You might try a really poor area of the world that's currently undergoing some kind of armed conflict. Somewhere in or near ISIS-controlled territory might work, or maybe some place in the area currently affected by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boko_Haram_insurgency\" target=\"_blank\">Boko Haram Insurgency</a>. Would deliberately preying on already desperate and endangered populations make the whole thing more awful? Yes, yes it would.<br /> <br /> Also, isn't there a condition where diablerie victims haunt your brain and drive you crazy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T23:28:15-07:00","id":858185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=858171#post858171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, isn't there a condition where diablerie victims haunt your brain and drive you crazy?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd take a Tainted condition instead of the usual Bestial/Competitive/Wanton conditions (if you succeeded on the Humanity check(s)) or instead of Guilty/Jaded (if you failed the Humanity check(s)).<br /> <br /> Can Tainted conditions stack? I feel like 45 of them in a row would make the character borderline unplayable. Your Storyteller might end up giving you an Amaranth Bane even if you succeeded just so you don't end up getting 45 beats (9 whopping EXP) in a row.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11527-hakamichi-kurloz-sir","name":"Hakamichi Kurloz, Sir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T00:20:35-07:00","id":858196,"title":"","content":"Ooh, that gives me a somewhat amusing idea...<br /> <br /> People can develop allergies over time as a result of overexposure to some substances. Latex is a good example; a lot of hospitals have phased out latex gloves entirely because employees who don't have latex allergies can actually get them as a result of the constant contact with airborne latex particles.<br /> <br /> Maybe somebody who commits diablerie too frequently could develop an <i>intolerance</i> to it. This presumably wouldn't be an actual physiological response, since vampires don't really have a functional biochemical physiology, but maybe the vampire's soul just couldn't take it anymore and would start to violently reject further attempts. Maybe you could even start suffering some sort of soul damage as a result, possibly modeled by temporarily gaining the &quot;soulless&quot; condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T00:42:18-07:00","id":858199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857632#post857632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had them as Ventrue, actually. Not that important, since they are dead (Final Death, barring the need/desire for a curve-ball) by now anyways. They were a historical figure used to flesh out some backstory and explain why to Domain is in the state it is now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yowza. That's a little interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11528-dangerus-muyoko-project","name":"Dangerus-Muyoko-Project","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T05:59:02-07:00","id":858299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857415#post857415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Daeva En Bloodline would without a doubt try this even if he might get caught. There from the Ancient Bloodline Book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Throw in the Coil of \u017diva, and even Detachment rolls and Humanity loss are no longer problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:15:46-07:00","id":997146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=858299#post858299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Throw in the Coil of \u017diva, and even Detachment rolls and Humanity loss are no longer problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the thread necromancy, but something I <i>just</i> realized: how would having a Neglatu involved affect things, since they can &quot;uplift&quot; Revenants without the Humanity loss? Wouldn't even need the Embrace chaining, since the one Neglatu could make/uplift a bunch of Revenants into BP 1 Kindred, then diablerize them (or the &quot;controller&quot; does) for XP. Humanity would still be risked by Killing and Diablerie (provided those can't be inured to with Banes). The Tainted Condition could be burned off with periodic Aggravated damage (and there should be plenty of blood from the process to spare for that).<br /> <br /> Thoughts on this &quot;refinement&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:08:27-07:00","id":997183,"title":"","content":"1 WEIRD TRICK TO RAISE BLOOD POTENCY. DISCOVERED BY A GANGREL. PRINCES HATE HIM!<br /> <br /> e: imagine starting a chronicle by waking up as a vampire in a room full of frenzying chained-up draugr while your blood-drenched sire looks up from his serial-maximum-soulmurder shipping chart and says &quot;don't worry- i mathed the whole thing out!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 11-02-2016, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T10:42:57-07:00","id":997235,"title":"","content":"My personal advice : Take your time and have other activities on the side.<br /> <br /> The warzone thing isn't a bad idea, but for other reasons. First, the vampire should target soldiers, mostly the kind that murder and pillage, it'll be way easier for someone to rationalize kidnapping a bunch of murderers than civilians who are already victims of those same people, so the humanity checks for kidnapping, dominating into embracing might get a small bonus. After all, this is pretty much public service at this point, right ? Right ?<br /> <br /> Second, I'd plan to do that within a year or so. During that time, I'd infiltrate a humanitarian organisation that is doing work there and use my powers to help them do a better work. I'd make friends, dominate some local politicians so they'd give the org money, dominate the warlords so they wouldn't attack the org or a nearby village, you know, use my powers for good, stay in touch with my humanity. That might help getting back some that I'll undoubtedly lose with that &quot;get higher BP&quot; business. You, know, it's really convenient to call the vampire who'll be doing that a complete hypocrite, but at the end of the day, did they now help so many people not doing stupidly with that ? Yeah, so they had an extracurricular project about diablerizing almost 50 people, but look, you don't get nothing for nothing.<br /> <br /> Of course, at the end of the day, you might end up with a powerful a shit vampire with the souls of 45 violent soldiers swirling inside their head. I mean at least it's consistent, you know ? You don't get haunted by the memories of a flower vendor, a single mother, a police officer, a tourist and so on. It helps staying focused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:00:38-07:00","id":997245,"title":"","content":"What is the Coil of Ziva? <br /> <br /> <br /> Also. Anyone interested in helping Develop or toss out ideas for a Bloodline for Diablerie that is not En? My ST wants me to create one for my serial diablerist and I will admit.. I am struggling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:04:30-07:00","id":997247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=997245#post997245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the Coil of Ziva?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also. Anyone interested in helping Develop or toss out ideas for a Bloodline for Diablerie that is not En? My ST wants me to create one for my serial diablerist and I will admit.. I am struggling.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's their modus operandi, and where do you want to go with them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:11:31-07:00","id":997251,"title":"","content":"He is a Daeva, but he hunts down bad vampires and eats them. He was the sheriff for a while, but that's what started this. It started to corrupt him because he began to eat the &quot;baddies&quot;<br /> <br /> He is generally morally on the right path, but more like Dexter. He thinks he is fixing the world by removing the bad apples. Or at least that's how it started. Usually uses Dominate or Majesty on them to see if they are truly horrible or not, then eats them if they are. He has focused on Staking them so they can't fight back.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Sorry for the thread Hijack, but it did seem sort of fitting for a serial diablerist bloodline in the fast track to elder via diablerie thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 11-02-2016, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:15:27-07:00","id":997254,"title":"","content":"Coil of Ziva is a diablerie-focused Coil from the preview document for Ordo Dracul's stuff in the upcoming book Secrets of the Covenants:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_J83T-t9g-87pvtUTKCZIJ2QQzCTOzUclkWJjsvb814/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_J83T-t9g-87pvtUTKCZIJ2QQzCTOzUclkWJjsvb814/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_J83T-t9g-87pvtUTKCZIJ2QQzCTOzUclkWJjsvb814/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_J83T-t9g-87pvtUTKCZIJ2QQzCTOzUclkWJjsvb814/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As for your bloodlines, there's really only three sources of inspiration in the existing material that I know of. Coil of Ziva, Coil of the Locust, and the En. Both the Coils are extremes. The Locust is just underwhelming to say the least while Ziva is so incredibly broken and over powerful I don't get how it managed to reach open development. I'd look at the first Coil of Ziva, Denying the Bane, as well as the Gifts of the Alu for inspiration. You said you didn't want to play an En, but their bloodline gifts are definitely fitting a diablerist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:21:01-07:00","id":997258,"title":"","content":"I wanted to play an En. When I hit 6 I asked if I could join it and my storyteller wanted me to create my own bloodline unique for my character ( I have now hit 10, through Diablerie, obviously) I brought to the table something that was extremely similar to the En, but she said she didn't want too much copying of something already there. So I am kind of lost!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:22:51-07:00","id":997259,"title":"","content":"Did your ST give any reason as for why you should create a new bloodline instead of joining the En bloodline?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:29:16-07:00","id":997270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=997259#post997259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did your ST give any reason as for why you should create a new bloodline instead of joining the En bloodline?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;To create something unique for my character&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:42:45-07:00","id":997277,"title":"","content":"The excuse I would give a player for not being an En is that it really feels like it was written as a bond villain bloodline (their weakness is that they underestimate their enemies) and not a player bloodline. That and because they are broken as hell. The &quot;you have to create something unique&quot; excuse sounds pretty flimsy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","user":"S. Brechen","date":". 11-02-2016, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:46:43-07:00","id":997281,"title":"","content":"Ehh... the point of the CofD is to play monsters. That includes so-called Bond villains. There's no reason that you can't play them unless you have a specific mindset you want in your players. I've seen the En run successfully several times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:51:56-07:00","id":997286,"title":"","content":"I am not saying that I had to get to 10 to get there.. I am saying she told me at 6 and I am now at 10 and still struggling to create something. I put those numbers in for my request to show you there has been quite some time in RL and in game since the request was first made. again, not to say I had to get to 10 to take this bloodline.<br /> <br /> I personally dont think that asking me to write something unique is a flimsy excuse. I am not even sure why it's an excuse. But it is just a task I have been struggling to complete on my own.<br /> <br /> the game still seems to be going strong. He is only one person and one person cant do everything. I was just asking for some help on a unique bloodline that is for a serial diablerist. Any ideas for actual bloodline gifts, banes, powers merits, anything would be helpful..<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#263238\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Gifts:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#263238\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> you can spend your Blood experience on vampire related powers. Though at a rate of 2/1.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#263238\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">you gain the normal discipline as well as a skill dot, if there are no disciplines to receive you instead gain three skills. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#263238\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Diablerie has become such second nature that it is now at a Humanity 3 and the tainted condition is halved. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#263238\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Immunity to Addictions<br /> <br /> Bane ideas:<br /> <br /> Soul Hungry. Any time the vampire fails a feeding frenzy they are compelled into Diablerie. The call of the soul overwhelms the vampire and they must consume it. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#263238\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Effect: Any time a vampire fails a normal Hunger frenzy check, treat that failure as a dramatic failure.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#263238\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Resolution: They must consume a soul in order to satiate their beast, reach a breaking point or be forced into Torpor </span></span><br /> <br /> Bane: Permanently Tainted<br /> <br /> Bane: Permanently Addicted to Diablerie<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 11-02-2016, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:56:26-07:00","id":997289,"title":"","content":"I have the same problem with it as most DnD GMs have with having chaotic evil characters. Ok, vampire is a &quot;gothic horror and so mature&quot; RPG, but I've seldom seen players play an evil character well. Generally, it's either a 12 year old thing or you get the urge to play a fucked up character and it gets old relatively fast. The entire morality system punishes you for being too bad anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T12:21:19-07:00","id":997302,"title":"","content":"Ideas:<br /> <br /> Since your vampire is committed to &quot;only eating the bad ones&quot;, I'd stick some sort of &quot;violates the rules&quot; criteria on being able to commit diablerie on a target. Possibly as a Bane, but maybe just flavor. If you really wanted it to sting, it might be a 11-Humanity penalty on all violent/aggressive actions against any Kindred that is not &quot;guilty&quot;.<br /> <br /> Other Bane Ideas: Vice gets replaced with those of your victims. Aspirations get replaced (like the former). [Either of those forces your character to take up the victim's goals, or sacrifice a Willpower source]<br /> <br /> Boons might be: No Breaking point for Diablerie (given the above constraint on valid targets). Able to &quot;borrow&quot; a Discipline for Blood Potency (of the victim) + Blood Potency (of your vampire) in nights.<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Vigor, Celerity, Majesty, Nightmare [I don't know the character's Disciplines, which would matter, but I'd think Nightmare would be fitting for a serial Diablerist]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T14:26:43-07:00","id":997370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=997302#post997302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideas:<br /> <br /> Since your vampire is committed to &quot;only eating the bad ones&quot;, I'd stick some sort of &quot;violates the rules&quot; criteria on being able to commit diablerie on a target. Possibly as a Bane, but maybe just flavor. If you really wanted it to sting, it might be a 11-Humanity penalty on all violent/aggressive actions against any Kindred that is not &quot;guilty&quot;.<br /> <br /> Other Bane Ideas: Vice gets replaced with those of your victims. Aspirations get replaced (like the former). [Either of those forces your character to take up the victim's goals, or sacrifice a Willpower source]<br /> <br /> Boons might be: No Breaking point for Diablerie (given the above constraint on valid targets). Able to &quot;borrow&quot; a Discipline for Blood Potency (of the victim) + Blood Potency (of your vampire) in nights.<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Vigor, Celerity, Majesty, Nightmare [I don't know the character's Disciplines, which would matter, but I'd think Nightmare would be fitting for a serial Diablerist]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for the ideas. I suppose I should mention this is 2E so no vice/virtue, but that does seem to have some interesting flavor, like Izombie where she gets a bit of their personality for a bit, like perhaps a second dirge.. though considering he often does it again before the tainted condition wears off... he would end up being bogged down with all the dirges.. I do like the thought though. I cant see how to make that work mechanically.<br /> <br /> I tossed around the no breaking point for Diablerie as well. I like it &quot;as long as he fits the code&quot; very Dexter.<br /> <br /> He currently has everything but Auspex,(cant find the mehket... lol ) though his highest are Majesty and Protean. I should mention upon diablerie you do get a dot in a discipline permanently. so borrowing. do you mean borrowing a second dot? Say I ate a mehket I could get 2 dots of Auspex, though 1 not permanently? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T18:33:50-07:00","id":997488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=997370#post997370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thank you for the ideas. I suppose I should mention this is 2E so no vice/virtue, but that does seem to have some interesting flavor, like Izombie where she gets a bit of their personality for a bit, like perhaps a second dirge.. though considering he often does it again before the tainted condition wears off... he would end up being bogged down with all the dirges.. I do like the thought though. I cant see how to make that work mechanically.<br /> <br /> I tossed around the no breaking point for Diablerie as well. I like it &amp;quot;as long as he fits the code&amp;quot; very Dexter.<br /> <br /> He currently has everything but Auspex,(cant find the mehket... lol ) though his highest are Majesty and Protean. I should mention upon diablerie you do get a dot in a discipline permanently. so borrowing. do you mean borrowing a second dot? Say I ate a mehket I could get 2 dots of Auspex, though 1 not permanently? <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no Vice, I forgot. You could just have it replace Aspirations, then. Maybe rolling over onto Masque/Dirge. Or temporarily acquiring the victim's Banes.<br /> <br /> As for borrowing Disciplines, I meant at the victim's rating. Powerful? Yes, but it is temporary. If you want to really leverage it, you need ro engage in repeated, frequent Amaranth. Which is a vicious cycle, at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T08:25:37-07:00","id":997716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=997488#post997488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, no Vice, I forgot. You could just have it replace Aspirations, then. Maybe rolling over onto Masque/Dirge. Or temporarily acquiring the victim's Banes.<br /> <br /> As for borrowing Disciplines, I meant at the victim's rating. Powerful? Yes, but it is temporary. If you want to really leverage it, you need ro engage in repeated, frequent Amaranth. Which is a vicious cycle, at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Borrowing the entire thing for a short period of time seems really neat! <br /> <br /> Also I really like the idea of getting urges to do something because that's what they wanted to do, but Since they are all really bad vampires.. the urge might to go murder rape torture some innocent person. &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> I am thinking more like a terrible urge to hook up with an old friend from HS or to appologize to some lady I dont even know... or to go party at such and such club even though I hate going there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T09:09:19-07:00","id":997735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=997716#post997716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I really like the idea of getting urges to do something because that's what they wanted to do, but Since they are all really bad vampires.. the urge might to go murder rape torture some innocent person. &gt;.&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the point, really. Either you indulge in the same dark behavior (proving yourself a hypocrite), or you deliberately abstain and cost yourself that source of Willpower. Or maybe one of their Aspirations wasn't all bad (like protecting their still living sibling), and then you wrestle with guilt and the question of whether they were really all that evil.<br /> <br /> It's up to the ST how much they want to twist the knife, and in which direction, with every Diablerie. <hr /><br /> Other Bloodline Boon idea: Maybe, as long as you replace one of your Aspirations (and/or Dirge) in this way, you aren't subject to the &quot;F you&quot; dice penalty for the Tainted Condition (at least, for that instance of the Tainted Condition - overload yourself with soulmurder and it comes back into play).<br /> <br /> Hmm. This is shaping up more and more like it might be worthwhile to name the Bloodline Sin-Eater or something (term confusion be damned).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-03-2016, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T15:09:58-07:00","id":997903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/857268-fast-track-to-elder-diablerie-scheme?p=857290#post857290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, the humanity loss is the easiest part to negate out of this, provided you can force/trick others to Embrace, which doesn't seem to be that hard for confused neonates...</div> </div> </div> </div>[Lie]<a href=\"http://smbc-comics.com/index.php?db=comics&amp;id=689#comic\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\">The only way to cure vampirism is to pass the curse to 10 others</span></a>[/Lie]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-03-2016, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:"